The map-membership solver still cannot refute the synthetic cell branch through an abstract map frame. The fixed call rule gives us a cleaner solution: at this loop head the local scope has exactly five names (`arr`, `first`, `previous`, `current`, `drops`) and parent `0`. I’m making that exact configuration part of the invariant. This also strengthens Gate A context containment and is why `current` was initialized before the loop.
