codex
The fixed semantics’ concrete `#branch(true/false)` rules do not symbolically split an unevaluated integer comparison, so the source-level `if` is the obstruction. I’m switching to the equivalent Python expression `drops = drops + (current < previous)` (and likewise for the closing edge). Python booleans participate in integer addition, and the supplied `MPY-INT` semantics defines that exact case. This removes control branching while preserving the algorithm for every integer list.
apply patch
